 in [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]place with one explicit write, never submits the prompt early, and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]never moves focus out of the field.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]7[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]prompt_task_links.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/prompt_task_links.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-oz[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-oz/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]bob capture-complete --task-links: (( in plain prose, with [/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]shared prose vectors[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]cli-task-links[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli-task-links: add a prose (( detector without capture-grammar checks, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the -T/--task-links option on capture-complete -L, byte-identical prose [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]trigger vectors, tests, and capture-complete docs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]block-id-prompt api.taskLinks v1: prose detector, ranked [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]session, and safe ID naming[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]bip-task-api[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli-task-links[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]bip-task-api: expose the existing (( engine as api.taskLinks v1. It adds[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the prose fieldAt detector replaying the shared vectors, a snapshot [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]session with ranked rows, guards (including subjects) and indexing [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]progress, and an editor-free validate/name write via vault.process or [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the open editor.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]proseField v2: the tasks mode of the LINK band, the NAME [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]stage, and the real-Obsidian spike[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-task-band[dim] · [dim][/dim]after bip-task-api[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-task-band: add the tasks mode to nav's proseField controller in new [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fragments (model, renderer, mode state machine). It covers the list and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]NAME stages, beforeinput-fed ID editing, the leftover (( hint, and API [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]v2, plus tests, preview states, a real-Obsidian spike, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]block-id-prompt docs section.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Task-bearing prompts S1–S12: subject guards, host safety, [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]prose lint[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]prompt-subjects[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-task-band[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]prompt-subjects: wire subjects for S1–S11 (S12 none) and audit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]picker-host key offering during NAME. It adds the per-family host-safety[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tests and extends the prose-field lint with subjects.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Intention Card, Record Card, and Task from email (S13–S15)[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]card-surfaces[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav-task-band[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]card-surfaces: make (( and NAME survive the Intention Card repaints and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]key ladder, the Record Card typed stages, and the (( field-mode link [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stage, and verify the email task modal.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold 